        "subject": "LU-19744 doc: document the llapi_ioctl(3) return contract",
        "message": "LU-19744 doc: document the llapi_ioctl(3) return contract\n\nllapi_ioctl(3) said the function returns 0 on success and a negative\nvalue on failure, but it returns the ioctl(2) result directly, so a\nfailure is -1 with errno set. The one exception is a negative fd,\nwhich returns -EBADF and sets errno to match.\n\nFixes: 594b780062db (\"LU-16634 misc: replace obsolete ioctl numbers\")\nSigned-off-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:Opus-5 llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: I18f941ebc492f7986d13175166b2a5e952d63671\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68261\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Arshad Hussain <arshad.hussain@aeoncomputing.com>\nReviewed-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\n"
      },
